win32u: IME window ownership and owner-group z-order notifications, as on Windows (Illustrator's New Document dialog)

Measured on Windows 11 (harnesses/swp-ownergroup.exe, his machine): a thread's default IME window is owned by its active
top-level window (and by the focus window's top level, across threads), and every SetWindowPos that touches z-order sends
WM_WINDOWPOSCHANGING to the whole owner group, other threads' windows included, waiting for them. Wine left IME windows unowned
and told only the window itself. Illustrator's New Document dialog relies on the wait: on Windows the hide waits on the
extension-panel process's IME window in Illustrator's group, Adobe's dispatcher builds the document inside the call, and the
dialog closes after the document appears. Under Wine it closed first and the home screen showed meanwhile.
Kill switches NEUTRON_IME_OWNER=0, NEUTRON_OWNER_GROUP=0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

--- a/dlls/win32u/imm.c
